# Frontend testing

## Stack

- Use Vitest, which is configured in the frontend workspace.
- Use React Testing Library for component behavior.
- The shared test setup loads `@testing-library/jest-dom/vitest`.
- Add `@testing-library/user-event`, MSW, or browser end-to-end tooling only
  when the confirmed product behavior needs it.

## Test behavior

- Prefer semantic queries such as `getByRole`, `getByLabelText`, and
  `getByText`.
- Test what users can see, enter, select, submit, and receive as feedback.
- Avoid tests coupled to implementation details, generated class names, or
  internal component state.
- Mock API boundaries instead of making real external requests.
- Test loading, error, empty, and inaccessible states when the feature has
  them.

## Scope

- Add or update tests in the same change as interactive behavior, data
  transformations, or UI regressions.
- Add browser end-to-end coverage only for critical flows confirmed by an
  approved specification.
- Do not add test-only production routes or public debugging data.

## Commands

```bash
npm run typecheck --workspace frontend
npm run lint --workspace frontend
npm run test --workspace frontend
npm run build --workspace frontend
```
